OpenWrt does not yet have official support for the R5C as it does the R4S. The custom version of OpenWrt released by FriendlyElec, which they call FriendlyWrt, does support the R5C and they post new builds frequently at the Firmware OEM link.

Download the file, decompress the image, and write it to a micro SD card using a tool like [[https://www.balena.io/etcher/|Balena Etcher]]. Then insert the micro SD card into the R5C, plug in power, and it'll boot the image. From there it can also be copied to the eMMC from the LuCI menu. Note FriendlyWrt uses 192.168.2.1 for their default device IP which can be changed in LuCI. Read the FriendlyElec wiki for more info on their image.

More details on -> [[:docs:guide-user:installation:installation_methods:sd_card|Install OpenWrt (sdcard explanation)]]
